Kindly use the below queries to fetch the historical execution statistics and query cost details for the mentioned stored procedures.
These queries will only read performance metadata from DMVs/Query Store and will NOT execute the stored procedures again.

---

1. Stored Procedure Execution Statistics

---

SELECT
DB_NAME(database_id) AS DatabaseName,
OBJECT_NAME(object_id, database_id) AS ProcedureName,
cached_time,
last_execution_time,
execution_count,
total_elapsed_time / 1000 AS TotalElapsedTime_ms,
(total_elapsed_time / execution_count) / 1000 AS AvgElapsedTime_ms,
total_worker_time / 1000 AS TotalCPU_ms,
(total_worker_time / execution_count) / 1000 AS AvgCPU_ms,
total_logical_reads,
total_logical_writes
FROM sys.dm_exec_procedure_stats
WHERE OBJECT_NAME(object_id, database_id) IN
(
'DPR_INS_MATM_VOUCHING_DATA',
'DPR_USERGENERATE_CSV_REPORT',
'DPR_GENERATE_CSV_REPORT',
'DPR_MATM_PAYMENT_PROCESSING'
)
ORDER BY last_execution_time DESC;

---

2. Query Store Runtime Statistics (Historical Details)

---

SELECT
OBJECT_NAME(qsq.object_id) AS ProcedureName,
qsp.plan_id,
qsrs.count_executions,
qsrs.avg_duration / 1000 AS AvgDuration_ms,
qsrs.max_duration / 1000 AS MaxDuration_ms,
qsrs.avg_cpu_time / 1000 AS AvgCPU_ms,
qsrs.avg_logical_io_reads AS AvgLogicalReads,
qsrs.avg_query_max_used_memory AS AvgMemoryUsageKB
FROM sys.query_store_query qsq
JOIN sys.query_store_plan qsp
ON qsq.query_id = qsp.query_id
JOIN sys.query_store_runtime_stats qsrs
ON qsp.plan_id = qsrs.plan_id
WHERE OBJECT_NAME(qsq.object_id) IN
(
'DPR_INS_MATM_VOUCHING_DATA',
'DPR_USERGENERATE_CSV_REPORT',
'DPR_GENERATE_CSV_REPORT',
'DPR_MATM_PAYMENT_PROCESSING'
)
ORDER BY qsrs.max_duration DESC;

---

3. Get Estimated Query Cost from Cached Execution Plans

---

SELECT
DB_NAME(st.dbid) AS DatabaseName,
OBJECT_NAME(st.objectid, st.dbid) AS ProcedureName,
qs.execution_count,
qs.total_elapsed_time / 1000 AS TotalElapsed_ms,
qs.total_worker_time / 1000 AS TotalCPU_ms,
qp.query_plan
FROM sys.dm_exec_query_stats qs
CROSS APPLY sys.dm_exec_sql_text(qs.sql_handle) st
CROSS APPLY sys.dm_exec_query_plan(qs.plan_handle) qp
WHERE OBJECT_NAME(st.objectid, st.dbid) IN
(
'DPR_INS_MATM_VOUCHING_DATA',
'DPR_USERGENERATE_CSV_REPORT',
'DPR_GENERATE_CSV_REPORT',
'DPR_MATM_PAYMENT_PROCESSING'
);

Note:

* Open the XML execution plan from the "query_plan" column.
* Check the "Estimated Subtree Cost" value from the execution plan.
* This represents the optimizer estimated query cost.

---

4. Long Running Queries from Last Week

---

SELECT TOP 20
OBJECT_NAME(st.objectid, st.dbid) AS ProcedureName,
qs.execution_count,
qs.total_elapsed_time / 1000 AS TotalElapsed_ms,
(qs.total_elapsed_time / qs.execution_count) / 1000 AS AvgElapsed_ms,
qs.total_worker_time / 1000 AS TotalCPU_ms,
qs.total_logical_reads,
qs.last_execution_time
FROM sys.dm_exec_query_stats qs
CROSS APPLY sys.dm_exec_sql_text(qs.sql_handle) st
WHERE OBJECT_NAME(st.objectid, st.dbid) IN
(
'DPR_INS_MATM_VOUCHING_DATA',
'DPR_USERGENERATE_CSV_REPORT',
'DPR_GENERATE_CSV_REPORT',
'DPR_MATM_PAYMENT_PROCESSING'
)
AND qs.last_execution_time >= DATEADD(DAY, -7, GETDATE())
ORDER BY AvgElapsed_ms DESC;

These queries can be safely executed on the client server to collect historical performance statistics and query cost details without rerunning the stored procedures.
